      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "978c3aec3b66831f5c8fe8dfa2af8e85b9060582",
            "subject": "LU-10948 mdt: grant write open locks without LOOKUP"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-06 04:17:29.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-16 16:41:18.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-10948 ldlm: age out idle cached write open handles",
        "message": "LU-10948 ldlm: age out idle cached write open handles\n\nA cached write open handle stays open on the MDT until its CW OPEN\nlock is cancelled, which for an idle file is the LRU age of 600s.\nUntil then the MDT would not see the close, so the file size update,\nthe changelog CLOSE record and actions taken at last close were\ndelayed by up to 10 minutes after the application closed the file.\n\nAdd a short-lived LRU list to the namespace, for unused locks that\nshould be cancelled sooner than the LRU age, in the order they were\nlast used.  ldlm_namespace_set_short_lru() sets a callback that picks\nthese locks and their maximum age.  The LRU scan moves the locks not\nused for that long to the head of the normal LRU list to be\ncancelled, marked LRU_SHORT_EXPIRED, so that they do not make the\nscan cancel a batch of other locks.  The oldest of these locks are\nalso used when the normal list is too short for an LRU cancel.\n\nMDC puts unused CW OPEN locks on that list, with the age set by\n`llite.*.opencache_max_ms` (60s by default), which is also how soon a\nfile must be opened again to count as hot.  The cached write handle\nis closed once the file is no longer hot.  llite passes the age to\neach MDC through LMV with KEY_OPENCACHE_MAX_MS, including MDTs added\nlater.  With opencache_max_ms=0, no file is hot, and these locks are\ncancelled at the next LRU scan.\n\nAdd sanity test_441b to check that a reused write handle stays\ncached and an idle one is closed.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanityn,sanity-hsm\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I58d0d1cf2a9c477af695051aec558a52023ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
